WEBVTT

1
00:00:01.410 --> 00:00:03.984
<v Examiner>Define drug addiction, and give an example.

2
00:00:03.984 --> 00:00:06.558
<v Examiner>How is addiction different from dependence?

3
00:00:06.558 --> 00:00:07.277
<v Examiner>Three marks.

4
00:00:07.727 --> 00:00:09.882
The hook: addiction is a behaviour.

5
00:00:09.882 --> 00:00:13.145
Craving, loss of control, and using despite the harm.

6
00:00:13.595 --> 00:00:14.253
Her slide.

7
00:00:14.253 --> 00:00:17.344
Addiction is a behavioural pattern of drug use.

8
00:00:17.344 --> 00:00:21.619
Overwhelming involvement in getting the drug, and using the drug.

9
00:00:21.619 --> 00:00:25.894
It impairs three functional systems: motivation and reward, mood,

10
00:00:25.894 --> 00:00:27.670
and behavioural inhibition.

11
00:00:27.670 --> 00:00:30.235
And there's a high tendency to relapse.

12
00:00:30.685 --> 00:00:34.722
Her formative test three, question five, asks for exactly this:

13
00:00:34.722 --> 00:00:36.900
a behavioural pattern of drug use,

14
00:00:36.900 --> 00:00:42.475
where the person experiences overwhelming involvement in getting the drug and using the

15
00:00:42.475 --> 00:00:42.795
drug.

16
00:00:42.795 --> 00:00:46.447
The wrong options are tolerance, a change of legal class,

17
00:00:46.447 --> 00:00:49.715
and the combined use of stimulants and depressants.

18
00:00:50.165 --> 00:00:50.919
The example.

19
00:00:50.919 --> 00:00:55.693
Someone who keeps using even after losing their job and their relationships,

20
00:00:55.693 --> 00:00:57.703
and who relapses after stopping.

21
00:00:57.703 --> 00:01:03.168
And her slide notes that the same behavioural pattern happens without a drug: gambling,

22
00:01:03.168 --> 00:01:04.927
disordered eating, shopping.

23
00:01:06.377 --> 00:01:08.362
The difference, in one line each.

24
00:01:08.362 --> 00:01:13.235
Addiction is behaviour: craving, loss of control, and continued use despite harm.

25
00:01:13.235 --> 00:01:17.386
Dependence is the body: withdrawal symptoms when the drug is stopped.

26
00:01:17.386 --> 00:01:21.476
You can be dependent without being addicted, like the daily inhaler.

27
00:01:21.476 --> 00:01:25.807
And she warned there are a lot of myths about addiction, so in the exam,

28
00:01:25.807 --> 00:01:27.071
stick to these words.

29
00:01:27.521 --> 00:01:28.022
<v Examiner>Once more.

30
00:01:28.022 --> 00:01:29.526
<v Examiner>Addiction, and the difference.

31
00:01:31.976 --> 00:01:34.816
Addiction: a behavioural pattern of drug use,

32
00:01:34.816 --> 00:01:38.604
with overwhelming involvement in getting and using the drug.

33
00:01:38.604 --> 00:01:43.969
It impairs motivation-reward, mood and behavioural inhibition, and relapse is likely.

34
00:01:43.969 --> 00:01:47.062
Someone who keeps using despite losing their job.

35
00:01:47.062 --> 00:01:51.796
The difference: addiction is craving, loss of control and use despite harm.

36
00:01:51.796 --> 00:01:54.952
Dependence is withdrawal when the drug is stopped.
